# Risk Detection Logic Improvements

I have improved the risk analysis logic to catch more high-risk clauses by making the regex patterns more flexible and robust.

## Changes
-   **Enhanced Regex Patterns**: Updated `RISK_PATTERNS` in [src/lib/mockAnalysis.ts](file:///c:/Users/GERSHOM%20DANI/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/tos-illuminator/src/lib/mockAnalysis.ts) to handle:
    -   Flexible word ordering (e.g., "sell your data" vs "data sell").
    -   Synonyms (e.g., "payment details", "user location").
    -   "Share your location" detection.
    -   "Mandatory arbitration" (adjective-noun) support.

## Verification Results

I ran a reproduction script with clauses that were previously missed or scored low. All now trigger High risk warnings.

| Text Clause | Previous Score | New Score | Risk Level |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| "We sell your data to third parties." | Low | **8** | **High** |
| "You agree to mandatory arbitration." | Low | **8** | **High** |
| "We collect your social security number." | **8** (Pass) | **8** | **High** |
| "We share your location with partners." | Low | **8** | **High** |

## How to Verify
1.  Open the application at [http://localhost:5173/](http://localhost:5173/).
2.  Paste any of the phrases above into the analyzer.
3.  Observe the **High Risk** badge and the red highlighting on the detected terms.
